WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.245
Easy Science. Why Is the Sky Blue?

00:00:03.245 --> 00:00:06.287
Look up on a clear day and the sky is blue.

00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:07.221
But why?

00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:12.801
Light from the sun looks white, but it is really made of many colors mixed together.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:20.122
You can see these colors in a rainbow: red, orange, yellow, green, blue and purple.

00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:22.017
Light travels in waves.

00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:24.261
Red light has long waves.

00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:26.547
Blue light has short waves.

00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:31.854
When sunlight comes into the air around the earth, it hits tiny bits of air.

00:00:31.854 --> 00:00:34.969
The long red waves pass through quite easily.

00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:39.682
But the short blue waves hit the air and are thrown in every direction.

00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:42.378
Blue light is sent all across the sky.

00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:47.077
So when you look up, blue light comes to your eyes from everywhere.

00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:50.265
Then why is the sky red and orange in the evening?

00:00:50.265 --> 00:00:52.465
At that time the sun is low.

00:00:52.465 --> 00:00:56.413
Its light has to travel through much more air to reach you.

00:00:56.413 --> 00:01:01.433
Most of the blue light is thrown away to the sides before it gets to your eyes.

00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:04.237
The red and orange light is what is left.

00:01:04.237 --> 00:01:07.868
So the same thing gives us blue days and red evenings.
